    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">50 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Behavioral pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 1: must know cold, with code</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>State</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">When an object behaves differently depending on what has happened to it so far, give each situation its own object and let those objects hand over to each other. Learn when a plain enum and a transition table are better, how State differs from Strategy, and why the TCP state machine is the example you already know by heart.</p>\n  <p class=\"small prereq\"><b>Before this page:</b> <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-interfaces\">Interfaces</a> (program to an interface), <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-oop-polymorphism\">Polymorphism</a> (one call, many bodies), and <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-class\">UML class diagrams</a> for the notation in the Structure picture (arrows and diamonds: <a href=\"{{BASE}}lld/lld-uml-relationships\">relationships</a>).</p>\n"
  },
